"firstVerse":7}],"words":[{"base":"H7198","lemma":"קֶ֫שֶׁת","tr":"qe·shet","gloss":"bow","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":76},{"base":"H1368","lemma":"גִּבּוֹר","tr":"gib·bor","gloss":"mighty man","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":159},{"base":"H7970","lemma":"שְׁלֹשִׁים","tr":"she·lo·shim","gloss":"thirty","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":172},{"base":"H3460","lemma":"יִשְׁמַעְיָ֫הוּ","tr":"yish·ma·yah","gloss":"Ishmaiah","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H6404","lemma":"פֶּ֫לֶט","tr":"pe·let","gloss":"Pelet","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H7586","lemma":"שָׁאוּל","tr":"sha·ul","gloss":"Saul","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":406},{"base":"H1294","lemma":"בְּרָכָה","tr":"be·ra·khah","gloss":"Beracah","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H3434","lemma":"יָשׇׁבְעָם","tr":"ya·shov·am","gloss":"Jashobeam","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H3231","lemma":"יָמַן","tr":"ya·man","gloss":"to go right","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"H8114","lemma":"שְׁמַרְיָ֫הוּ","tr":"she·mar·yah","gloss":"Shemariah","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":4}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"JDG","chapter":3,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"And again they cried out to the LORD, and He raised up Ehud son of Gera, a left-handed Benjamite, as their deliverer. So they sent him with tribute to Eglon king of Moab.","from":2},{"book":"JDG","chapter":20,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Among all these soldiers there were 700 select left-handers, each of whom could sling a stone at a hair without missing.","from":2},{"book":"DEU","chapter":32,"verse":32,"verseEnd":32,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"But their vine is from the vine of Sodom and from the fields of Gomorrah. Their grapes are poisonous; their clusters are bitter.","from":1},{"book":"JOS","chapter":9,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"But the people of Gibeon, having heard what Joshua had done to Jericho and Ai,","from":4},{"book":"JOS","chapter":9,"verse":17,"verseEnd":23,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"So the Israelites set out and on the third day arrived at their cities—Gibeon, Chephirah, Beeroth, and Kiriath-jearim. But the Israelites did not attack them, because the leaders of the congregation had sworn an oath to them by the LORD, the God of Israel. And the whole congregation grumbled against the leaders. All the leaders answered, “We have sworn an oath to them by the LORD, the God of Israel, and now we cannot touch them. This is how we will treat them: We will let them live, so that no wrath will fall on us because of the oath we swore to them.” They continued, “Let them live, but let them be woodcutters and water carriers for the whole congregation.” So the leaders kept their promise.","from":4},{"book":"JOS","chapter":15,"verse":36,"verseEnd":36,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Shaaraim, Adithaim, and Gederah (or Gederothaim)—fourteen cities, along with their villages.","from":4},{"book":"JOS","chapter":15,"verse":58,"verseEnd":58,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Halhul, Beth-zur, Gedor,","from":7},{"book":"1SA","chapter":11,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"When the messengers came to Gibeah of Saul and relayed these words in the hearing of the people, they all wept aloud.","from":3}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"kings-prophets","title":"Kings, prophets and the house of David","people":2}]},"8-15":{"people":[{"id":"david-h1732","name":"David","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"eliab-h0446j","name":"Eliab","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"ezer-h5829h","name":"Ezer","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"obadiah-h5662l","name":"Obadiah","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"jeremiah-h3414j","name":"Jeremiah","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"mishmannah-h4925","name":"Mishmannah","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"attai-h6262h","name":"Attai","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"eliel-h0447l","name":"Eliel","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"elzabad-h0443g","name":"Elzabad","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"johanan-h3076h","name":"Johanan","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"jeremiah-h3414k","name":"Jeremiah","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"machbannai-h4344","name":"Machbannai","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":13}],"places":[{"id":"jordan-h3383","name":"Jordan","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":15}],"words":[{"base":"H3414","lemma":"יִרְמְיָ֫הוּ","tr":"yir·me·yah","gloss":"Jeremiah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":147},{"base":"H0443","lemma":"אֶלְזָבָד","tr":"el·za·vad","gloss":"Elzabad","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H6635","lemma":"צָבָא","tr":"tsa·va","gloss":"army","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":484},{"base":"H1415","lemma":"גָּדָה","tr":"ga·dah","gloss":"bank","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"H6262","lemma":"עַתַּי","tr":"at·tay","gloss":"Attai","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"H5829","lemma":"עֵ֫זֶר","tr":"e·zer","gloss":"Ezer","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"H7218","lemma":"רֹאשׁ","tr":"rosh","gloss":"head","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":599},{"base":"H0428","lemma":"אֵ֫לֶּה","tr":"el·leh","gloss":"these","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":746},{"base":"H0447","lemma":"אֱלִיאֵל","tr":"e·li·el","gloss":"Eliel","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":10},{"base":"H3076","lemma":"יְהוֹחָנָן","tr":"ye·ho·cha·nan","gloss":"Johanan","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":11}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"2SA","chapter":2,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"The three sons of Zeruiah were there: Joab, Abishai, and Asahel. Now Asahel was fleet of foot like a wild gazelle,","from":8},{"book":"JOS","chapter":3,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Now the Jordan overflows its banks throughout the harvest season. But as soon as the priests carrying the ark reached the Jordan and their feet touched the waterʼs edge,","from":15},{"book":"LEV","chapter":26,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Five of you will pursue a hundred, and a hundred of you will pursue ten thousand, and your enemies will fall by the sword before you.","from":14},{"book":"DEU","chapter":32,"verse":30,"verseEnd":30,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"How could one man pursue a thousand, or two put ten thousand to flight, unless their Rock had sold them, unless the LORD had given them up?","from":14},{"book":"JOS","chapter":4,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"When the priests carrying the ark of the covenant of the LORD came up out of the Jordan and their feet touched the dry land, the waters of the Jordan returned to their course and overflowed all the banks as before.","from":15},{"book":"1SA","chapter":23,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And David stayed in the wilderness strongholds and in the hill country of the Wilderness of Ziph. Day after day Saul searched for him, but God would not deliver David into his hand.","from":8},{"book":"1SA","chapter":23,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And David went up from there and lived in the strongholds of En-gedi.","from":8},{"book":"1SA","chapter":24,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"So David gave his oath to Saul. Then Saul returned home, but David and his men went up to the stronghold.","from":8}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"16-18":{"people":[{"id":"david-h1732","name":"David","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":3,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"benjamin-h1144g","name":"Benjamin","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"amasai-h6022h","name":"Amasai","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"jesse-h3448","name":"Jesse","kind":"person","brief":"David's father","count":1,"firstVerse":18}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H7965","lemma":"שָׁלוֹם","tr":"sha·lom","gloss":"peace","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":237},{"base":"H5826","lemma":"עָזַר","tr":"a·zar","gloss":"to help","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":81},{"base":"H1732","lemma":"דָּוִד","tr":"da·vid","gloss":"David","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":1075},{"base":"H6022","lemma":"עֲמָשַׂי","tr":"a·ma·say","gloss":"Amasai","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"H7218","lemma":"רֹאשׁ","tr":"rosh","gloss":"head","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":599},{"base":"H9031","lemma":"ךָּ","tr":"ka","gloss":"you","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":727},{"base":"H4679","lemma":"מְצָד","tr":"me·tsad","gloss":"stronghold","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":11},{"base":"H7411","lemma":"רָמָה","tr":"ra·mah","gloss":"to shoot","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":12},{"base":"H6901","lemma":"קָבַל","tr":"qa·val","gloss":"to receive","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":13},{"base":"H0518","lemma":"אִם","tr":"im","gloss":"if","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":1067}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"JDG","chapter":6,"verse":34,"verseEnd":34,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"So the Spirit of the LORD came upon Gideon, who blew the ramʼs horn and rallied the Abiezrites behind him.","from":18},{"book":"JDG","chapter":3,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"The Spirit of the LORD came upon him, and he became Israelʼs judge and went out to war. And the LORD delivered Cushan-rishathaim king of Aram into the hand of Othniel, who prevailed against him.","from":18},{"book":"2SA","chapter":17,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Absalom had appointed Amasa over the army in place of Joab. Amasa was the son of a man named Ithra, the Ishmaelite who had married Abigail, the daughter of Nahash and sister of Zeruiah the mother of Joab.","from":18},{"book":"JHN","chapter":6,"verse":67,"verseEnd":67,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"So Jesus asked the Twelve, “Do you want to leave too?”","from":18},{"book":"JHN","chapter":6,"verse":68,"verseEnd":68,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"Simon Peter replied, “Lord, to whom would we go? You have the words of eternal life.","from":18},{"book":"GEN","chapter":31,"verse":42,"verseEnd":42,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"If the God of my father, the God of Abraham and the Fear of Isaac, had not been with me, surely by now you would have sent me away empty-handed. But God has seen my affliction and the toil of my hands, and last night He rendered judgment.”","from":17},{"book":"GEN","chapter":31,"verse":53,"verseEnd":53,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"May the God of Abraham and the God of Nahor, the God of their father, judge between us.” So Jacob swore by the Fear of his father Isaac.","from":17},{"book":"JDG","chapter":13,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And the Spirit of the LORD began to stir him at Mahaneh-dan, between Zorah and Eshtaol.","from":18}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"royal-line","title":"The royal line: Judah to David to Jesus","people":2},{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2},{"id":"judges-era","title":"Judges era and the road to David","people":2}]},"19-22":{"people":[{"id":"david-h1732","name":"David","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":3,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"manasseh-h4519g","name":"Manasseh","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":2,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"saul-h7586g","name":"Saul","kind":"person","brief":"King of Israel,","count":1,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"adnah-h5734g","name":"Adnah","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"elihu-h0453h","name":"Elihu","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"jediael-h3043i","name":"Jediael","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"jozabad-h3107i","name":"Jozabad","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"jozabad-h3107j","name":"Jozabad","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"michael-h4317m","name":"Michael","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"zillethai-h6769h","name":"Zillethai","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":1,"firstVerse":20}],"places":[{"id":"philistia-h6429","name":"Philistia","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"ziklag-h6860","name":"Ziklag","kind":"place","brief":"In Philistia","count":1,"firstVerse":20}],"words":[{"base":"H5826","lemma":"עָזַר","tr":"a·zar","gloss":"to help","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":81},{"base":"H4519","lemma":"מְנַשֶּׁה","tr":"me·nash·sheh","gloss":"Manasseh","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":146},{"base":"H3107","lemma":"יוֹזָבָד","tr":"yo·za·vad","gloss":"Jozacar","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":11},{"base":"H5307","lemma":"נָפַל","tr":"na·phal","gloss":"to fall: fall","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":434},{"base":"H1732","lemma":"דָּוִד","tr":"da·vid","gloss":"David","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":1075},{"base":"H4264","lemma":"מַחֲנֶה","tr":"ma·cha·neh","gloss":"camp","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":215},{"base":"H6430","lemma":"פְּלִשְׁתִּי","tr":"pe·lish·ti","gloss":"Philistine","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":288},{"base":"H5734","lemma":"עַדְנָה","tr":"ad·nah","gloss":"Adnah","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H6769","lemma":"צִלְּתַי","tr":"tsil·l·tay","gloss":"Zillethai","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H7586","lemma":"שָׁאוּל","tr":"sha·ul","gloss":"Saul","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":406}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"GEN","chapter":32,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"When Jacob saw them, he said, “This is the camp of God.” So he named that place Mahanaim.","from":22},{"book":"EXO","chapter":18,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Furthermore, select capable men from among the people—God-fearing, trustworthy men who are averse to dishonest gain. Appoint them over the people as leaders of thousands, of hundreds, of fifties, and of tens.","from":20},{"book":"DEU","chapter":1,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"So I took the leaders of your tribes, wise and respected men, and appointed them as leaders over you—as commanders of thousands, of hundreds, of fifties, and of tens, and as officers for your tribes.","from":20},{"book":"DEU","chapter":33,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"His majesty is like a firstborn bull, and his horns are like those of a wild ox. With them he will gore the nations, even to the ends of the earth. Such are the myriads of Ephraim, and such are the thousands of Manasseh.”","from":20},{"book":"JOS","chapter":5,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"“Neither,” He replied. “I have now come as Commander of the LORDʼs army.” Then Joshua fell facedown in reverence and asked Him, “What does my Lord have to say to His servant?”","from":22},{"book":"1SA","chapter":29,"verse":2,"verseEnd":4,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"As the Philistine leaders marched out eith their units of hundreds and thousands, David and his men marched behind them with Achish. Then the commanders of the Philistines asked, “What about these Hebrews?” Achish replied, “Is this not David, the servant of King Saul of Israel? He has been with me all these days, even years, and from the day he defected until today I have found no fault in him.” But the commanders of the Philistines were angry with Achish and told him, “Send that man back and let him return to the place you assigned him. He must not go down with us into battle only to become our adversary during the war. What better way for him to regain the favor of his master than with the heads of our men?","from":19},{"book":"1SA","chapter":29,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"So David and his men got up early in the morning to return to the land of the Philistines. And the Philistines went up to Jezreel.","from":20},{"book":"1SA","chapter":30,"verse":1,"verseEnd":17,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"On the third day David and his men arrived in Ziklag, and the Amalekites had raided the Negev, attacked Ziklag, and burned it down. They had taken captive the women and all who were there, both young and old. They had not killed anyone, but had carried them off as they went on their way. When David and his men came to the city, they found it burned down and their wives and sons and daughters taken captive. So David and the troops with him lifted up their voices and wept until they had no strength left to weep. Davidʼs two wives, Ahinoam of Jezreel and Abigail the widow of Nabal of Carmel, had been taken captive.","from":21}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"kings-prophets","title":"Kings, prophets and the house of David","people":2}]},"23-37":{"people":[{"id":"david-h1732","name":"David","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":2,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"saul-h7586g","name":"Saul","kind":"person","brief":"King of Israel,","count":2,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"simeon-h8095g","name":"Simeon","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"levi-h3878","name":"Levi","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"aaron-h0175","name":"Aaron","kind":"person","brief":"High Priest","count":1,"firstVerse":27},{"id":"jehoiada-h3077g","name":"Jehoiada","kind":"person","brief":"Father of warrior Benaiah","count":1,"firstVerse":27},{"id":"zadok-h6659g","name":"Zadok","kind":"person","brief":"A High Priest","count":1,"firstVerse":28},{"id":"benjamin-h1144g","name":"Benjamin","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":29},{"id":"ephraim-h0669g","name":"Ephraim","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":1,"firstVerse":30},{"id":"manasseh-h4519g","name":"Manasseh","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":2,"firstVerse":31},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":32},{"id":"issachar-h3485g","name":"Issachar","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":32},{"id":"zebulun-h2074","name":"Zebulun","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":33},{"id":"naphtali-h5321g","name":"Naphtali","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":34},{"id":"asher-h0836","name":"Asher","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":36},{"id":"reuben-h7205","name":"Reuben","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":37}],"places":[{"id":"hebron-h2275a","name":"Hebron","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"dan-h1835g","name":"Dan","kind":"place","brief":"In Dan","count":1,"firstVerse":35},{"id":"jordan-h3383","name":"Jordan","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":37}],"words":[{"base":"H0505","lemma":"אֶ֫לֶף","tr":"e·leph","gloss":"thousand","lang":"h","inPassage":13,"uses":506},{"base":"H3967","lemma":"מֵאָה","tr":"me·ah","gloss":"hundred","lang":"h","inPassage":8,"uses":581},{"base":"H6635","lemma":"צָבָא","tr":"tsa·va","gloss":"army","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":484},{"base":"H4421","lemma":"מִלְחָמָה","tr":"mil·cha·mah","gloss":"battle","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":319},{"base":"H8083","lemma":"שְׁמֹנֶה","tr":"she·mo·neh","gloss":"eight","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":109},{"base":"H4480","lemma":"מִן־","tr":"min","gloss":"from","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":1187},{"base":"H6242","lemma":"עֶשְׂרִים","tr":"es·rim","gloss":"twenty","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":315},{"base":"H6186","lemma":"עָרַךְ","tr":"a·rakh","gloss":"to arrange","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":75},{"base":"H1368","lemma":"גִּבּוֹר","tr":"gib·bor","gloss":"mighty man","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":159},{"base":"H8337","lemma":"שֵׁשׁ","tr":"shesh","gloss":"six","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":216}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"EPH","chapter":5,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":16,"source":"both","text":"Therefore do not be foolish, but understand what the Lordʼs will is.","from":32},{"book":"LUK","chapter":12,"verse":56,"verseEnd":56,"votes":14,"source":"openbible","text":"You hypocrites! You know how to interpret the appearance of the earth and sky. Why donʼt you know how to interpret the present time?","from":32},{"book":"LUK","chapter":12,"verse":57,"verseEnd":57,"votes":14,"source":"openbible","text":"And why donʼt you judge for yourselves what is right?","from":32},{"book":"EST","chapter":1,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":13,"source":"both","text":"Then the king consulted the wise men who knew the times, for it was customary for him to confer with the experts in law and justice.","from":32},{"book":"ISA","chapter":33,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":12,"source":"both","text":"He will be the sure foundation for your times, a storehouse of salvation, wisdom, and knowledge. The fear of the LORD is Zionʼs treasure.","from":32},{"book":"MAT","chapter":16,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"and in the morning, ‘Today it will be stormy, for the sky is red and overcast.’ You know how to interpret the appearance of the sky, but not the signs of the times.","from":32},{"book":"ECC","chapter":7,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"Wisdom makes the wise man stronger than ten rulers in a city.","from":32},{"book":"PRO","chapter":14,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"The wisdom of the prudent is to discern his way, but the folly of fools deceives them.","from":32}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":10},{"id":"kings-prophets","title":"Kings, prophets and the house of David","people":3},{"id":"royal-line","title":"The royal line: Judah to David to Jesus","people":2}]},"38-40":{"people":[{"id":"david-h1732","name":"David","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":2,"firstVerse":38},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":2,"firstVerse":38},{"id":"issachar-h3485g","name":"Issachar","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":40},{"id":"naphtali-h5321g","name":"Naphtali","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":40},{"id":"zebulun-h2074","name":"Zebulun","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":40}],"places":[{"id":"hebron-h2275a","name":"Hebron","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":38}],"words":[{"base":"H1732","lemma":"דָּוִד","tr":"da·vid","gloss":"David","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":1075},{"base":"H1241","lemma":"בָּקָר","tr":"ba·qar","gloss":"cattle","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":183},{"base":"H4427","lemma":"מָלַךְ","tr":"ma·lakh","gloss":"to reign","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":348},{"base":"H6778","lemma":"צַמּוּק","tr":"tsam·muq","gloss":"cluster","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"H1690","lemma":"דְּבֵלָה","tr":"de·ve·lah","gloss":"fig cake","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"H1571","lemma":"גַּם","tr":"gam","gloss":"also","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":769},{"base":"H5737","lemma":"עָדַר","tr":"a·dar","gloss":"to help","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":11},{"base":"H7058","lemma":"קֶ֫מַח","tr":"qe·mach","gloss":"flour","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":14},{"base":"H6505","lemma":"פֶּ֫רֶד","tr":"pe·red","gloss":"mule","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":15},{"base":"H4634","lemma":"מַעֲרָכָה","tr":"ma·a·ra·khah","gloss":"rank","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":19}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1SA","chapter":25,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Then Abigail hurried and took two hundred loaves of bread, two skins of wine, five butchered sheep, five seahs of roasted grain, a hundred clusters of raisins, and two hundred cakes of figs. She loaded them on donkeys","from":40},{"book":"GEN","chapter":26,"verse":30,"verseEnd":30,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"So Isaac prepared a feast for them, and they ate and drank.","from":39},{"book":"GEN","chapter":31,"verse":54,"verseEnd":54,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then Jacob offered a sacrifice on the mountain and invited his relatives to eat a meal. And after they had eaten, they spent the night on the mountain.","from":39},{"book":"GEN","chapter":49,"verse":8,"verseEnd":10,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Judah, your brothers shall praise you. Your hand shall be on the necks of your enemies; your fatherʼs sons shall bow down to you. Judah is a young lion— my son, you return from the prey. Like a lion he crouches and lies down; like a lioness, who dares to rouse him? The scepter will not depart from Judah, nor the staff from between his feet, until Shiloh comes and the allegiance of the nations is his.","from":38},{"book":"2SA","chapter":6,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then he distributed to every man and woman among the multitude of Israel a loaf of bread, a date cake, and a raisin cake. And all the people departed, each to his own home.","from":39},{"book":"2SA","chapter":16,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"When David had gone a little beyond the summit, Ziba the servant of Mephibosheth was there to meet him. He had a pair of saddled donkeys loaded with two hundred loaves of bread, a hundred clusters of raisins, a hundred summer fruits, and a skin of wine.","from":40},{"book":"2SA","chapter":17,"verse":27,"verseEnd":29,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"When David came to Mahanaim, he was met by Shobi son of Nahash from Rabbah of the Ammonites, Machir son of Ammiel from Lo-debar, and Barzillai the Gileadite from Rogelim. They brought beds, basins, and earthen vessels, as well as wheat, barley, flour, roasted grain, beans, lentils, honey, curds, sheep, and cheese from the herd for David and his people to eat. For they said, “The people have become hungry, exhausted, and thirsty in the wilderness.”","from":40},{"book":"2SA","chapter":19,"verse":42,"verseEnd":42,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And all the men of Judah replied to the men of Israel, “We did this because the king is our relative. Why does this anger you? Have we ever eaten at the kingʼs expense or received anything for ourselves?”","from":39}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":4}]}}